This program is also quite simple as was one of my earliest practices with python.
The program may be run with python mario.py
The user will then be prompted for a height, h, which must be an integer between 1 and 8, including 1 and 8.
Once a valid height is entered, the program uses nested for loops to print the pyramid of height h, provided by the user.
The outer loop iterates over each row of the pyramid, and the inner loops print the spaces and hashes for each row.
The first inner loop prints the spaces before the hashes in each row, the number of spaces decreases by h - i - 1, where h is height and i is the current row number.
The second inner loop prints the hashes in each row, the number of hashes increases down the pyramid by i + 1, where i is the current row number.
Finally, print is called to print the pyramid.
